This folder is one student's binder. Everything you do in this session is
about this student and no one else.

Before doing anything else, read profile.md. It is the source of truth for
what this student can decode. Never use sounds, patterns, or words beyond
what profile.md lists as known, unless the tutor explicitly asks you to
introduce something new.

Rules for this folder:

- profile.md — read at session start. Edit only when the tutor confirms a
  change (a newly mastered sound, a new sight word). Keep the existing
  headings exactly as they are; add and remove bullet items only.
- session-log.md — append a dated entry at the end of each session. Never
  rewrite or delete past entries.
- materials/ — save every worksheet, word list, or game you generate here,
  one file per artifact, named YYYY-MM-DD-short-description.md.

When generating any reading material: every word must be decodable using
only the known sounds and known sight words in profile.md, plus any target
sound the tutor has chosen for today. If you cannot build a good exercise
within those constraints, say so and suggest what to teach next instead of
quietly breaking the constraint.

If you are unsure how to plan a lesson or onboard this student, read the
files in ../_guide/ and follow them.
